course: dictionary
lesson: 2925
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so you must look at the context to know which one is right. The context is the words and sentences around the word. «Every evening she lies across Sam's bedroom door like a furry draught excluder.» A draught excluder keeps cold air out, so here a draught is a current of cold air.
explain: Draught can also be a game. «In checkers (draughts in the UK), you must jump when you can in standard rules, and a piece reaching the far row is crowned king.» Here draughts is a board game for two players, and each round flat piece is called a draught.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Let's play a cold air after tea» makes no sense, so draughts must mean the game here. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
fact: Draught is a noun meaning a current of cold air in a room, as in «There's a draught from the window».
fact: In the UK, draughts is a board game for two players, called checkers in the US.
fact: A draught can also be a long drink taken in one go, as in «a long draught of water».
fact: Draught beer is beer served from a barrel, not from a bottle.
fact: Draught is the UK spelling; in the US the word is spelled draft.
exercise: «Let's play draughts after tea.» What is draughts? | A cold current of air | Beer served from a barrel | *A board game for two players | A long drink of water
exercise: «Give me a long draught of water, please.» What does draught mean here? | A round flat game piece | The depth a ship needs to float | *A big swallow of a drink | Cold air from a window
exercise: «There's a draught from the window, so shut it.» What does draught mean here? | A drink taken in one go | A game for two players | *A current of cold air | Beer served from a barrel
test: «Sam's door has a furry draught excluder.» What does draught mean in this sentence? | A board game | A drink in one go | Beer served from a barrel | *Cold air moving into a room
test: Which is the US spelling of the word draught? | Drawt | Draugt | *Draft | Drought
exam: What does «draught beer» mean? | A long drink of water | *Beer served from a barrel, not a bottle | A game for two players | A cold wind through a door
